## 4. Configuration

### 4.1 Check the current RDMA mode

```bash
oc get sriovnetworknodestates -n openshift-sriov-network-operator -o yaml | grep rdmaMode
```

Expected output on the current cluster:

```
rdmaMode: shared
```

| Mode | Behaviour | When to use |
|---|---|---|
| `shared` (default) | All RDMA devices live in the host network namespace; the device plugin injects the correct `/dev/infiniband/*` character devices into each pod | Standard choice; works for almost all workloads |
| `exclusive` | Each pod sees only the RDMA device bound to its own VF (RDMA network namespace isolation) | Strict multi-tenant isolation requirements |

Switching to `exclusive` requires a node reboot. Only change it if there is a specific isolation requirement:

```yaml
apiVersion: sriovnetwork.openshift.io/v1
kind: SriovNetworkPoolConfig
metadata:
  name: rdma-exclusive
  namespace: openshift-sriov-network-operator
spec:
  rdmaMode: exclusive
  nodeSelector:
    matchLabels:
      feature.node.kubernetes.io/network-sriov.capable: "true"
```

### 4.2 Create the RDMA node policy

Rules that must be respected:

- `deviceType` must be `netdevice` – `isRdma: true` with `vfio-pci` is rejected
- `numVfs` must be **identical** on every policy that targets the same PF (16 on `ens1f2`)
- VF ranges must not overlap with existing policies (`ens1f2#0-3` and `ens1f2#4-8` are in use)
- Do not set `mtu` in the node policy (known issue from OCP 4.14.30 onwards; set MTU elsewhere if needed)

`sriov-rdma-node-policy.yaml`:

```yaml
apiVersion: sriovnetwork.openshift.io/v1
kind: SriovNetworkNodePolicy
metadata:
  name: policy-ens1f2-rdma
  namespace: openshift-sriov-network-operator
spec:
  resourceName: rdma_sriov_net
  nodeSelector:
    feature.node.kubernetes.io/network-sriov.capable: "true"
  priority: 99
  numVfs: 16
  nicSelector:
    vendor: "8086"
    deviceID: "1593"
    pfNames: ["ens1f2#9-12"]
  deviceType: netdevice
  isRdma: true
  linkType: eth
```

Apply:

```bash
oc apply -f sriov-rdma-node-policy.yaml
```

Because `numVfs` is unchanged, the operator only rebinds VFs 9–12; the node should not need a full VF re-creation, but it may still drain and reboot depending on the operator version. Monitor:

```bash
oc get sriovnetworknodestates -n openshift-sriov-network-operator
# wait for SYNC STATUS = Succeeded and CURRENT SYNC STATE = Idle on all nodes
```

Confirm the new resource is advertised:

```bash
oc describe nodes | grep rdma_sriov_net
#   openshift.io/rdma_sriov_net:   4
```

### 4.3 Create the SriovNetwork

`sriov-rdma-network.yaml`:

```yaml
apiVersion: sriovnetwork.openshift.io/v1
kind: SriovNetwork
metadata:
  name: rdma-net
  namespace: openshift-sriov-network-operator
spec:
  resourceName: rdma_sriov_net
  networkNamespace: rdma-app          # namespace where the RDMA pods run
  vlan: 300                           # RoCE VLAN, if tagged; remove if untagged
  spoofChk: "off"
  trust: "on"
  ipam: |
    {
      "type": "whereabouts",
      "range": "192.168.30.0/24",
      "exclude": ["192.168.30.1/32"]
    }
```

- `trust: "on"` allows the VF to set its own priority / VLAN tags, which PFC relies on
- `spoofChk: "off"` avoids drops when the RDMA stack uses the VF's own MAC with different priorities

Apply and verify the NetworkAttachmentDefinition was generated:

```bash
oc apply -f sriov-rdma-network.yaml
oc get net-attach-def -n rdma-app
# rdma-net
```

### 4.4 Deploy an RDMA pod

The container image must contain the RDMA userspace stack (`rdma-core`, `libibverbs`, `librdmacm`) and, for testing, `perftest`.

`rdma-test-pod.yaml`:

```yaml
apiVersion: v1
kind: Pod
metadata:
  name: rdma-test
  namespace: rdma-app
  annotations:
    k8s.v1.cni.cncf.io/networks: rdma-net
spec:
  containers:
  - name: perftest
    image: <registry>/rdma-perftest:latest
    command: ["sleep", "infinity"]
    securityContext:
      capabilities:
        add: ["IPC_LOCK"]            # required to pin memory for RDMA
    resources:
      requests:
        openshift.io/rdma_sriov_net: "1"
        cpu: "2"
        memory: "4Gi"
      limits:
        openshift.io/rdma_sriov_net: "1"
        cpu: "2"
        memory: "4Gi"
```

`IPC_LOCK` is mandatory. Without it `ibv_reg_mr` fails because the process cannot lock memory. Set `requests = limits` so the pod is Guaranteed QoS.

Deploy one pod per node (change the name) for cross-node testing:

```bash
oc apply -f rdma-test-pod.yaml
oc get pod -n rdma-app -o wide
```

