## 5. Verification

### 5.1 On the node

```bash
ssh core@master1.lab4.srib-lab-ocp.lan

# irdma devices for the RDMA VFs
rdma link show
# link rocep17s0f2v9/1 state ACTIVE physical_state LINK_UP netdev ens1f2v9
# ...

ibv_devices
lsmod | grep irdma
```

### 5.2 Inside the pod

```bash
oc exec -n rdma-app rdma-test -- ls /dev/infiniband
# rdma_cm  uverbs0

oc exec -n rdma-app rdma-test -- ibv_devinfo
# hca_id: rocep17s0f2v9
#   transport: InfiniBand (0)
#   ...
#   port: 1
#     state: PORT_ACTIVE (4)
#     link_layer: Ethernet

oc exec -n rdma-app rdma-test -- show_gids
# pick the GID index for RoCE v2 on the correct IPv4 address
```

### 5.3 Bandwidth and latency between two nodes

Server pod:

```bash
ib_write_bw -d rocep17s0f2v9 -F --report_gbits
```

Client pod (replace `<server-ip>` with the server pod's RDMA interface IP):

```bash
ib_write_bw -d rocep17s0f2v9 -F --report_gbits <server-ip>
ib_write_lat -d rocep17s0f2v9 -F <server-ip>
```

Expected on 25 GbE: roughly 22–23 Gb/s and 3–5 µs write latency. Also run `-q 4` (multiple QPs) to confirm throughput holds under parallel streams; if it drops sharply, PFC is not working on the switch.

